<title>FRANCE: Eutelsat picks Arianespace for W3 satellite launch.</title>
<headline>Eutelsat picks Arianespace for W3 satellite launch.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Eutelsat consortium said on Tuesday it has chosen Arianespace to launch its Eutelsat W3 telecommunications satellite, the third in the &quot;W&quot; series for the European Telecommunications Satellite Organisation.</p>
<p>The contract brings to five the number of satellites to be launched by Arianespace for Eutelsat, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>W3 will be built by state-owned Aerospatiale at its factory in Cannes on the French Riviera. Each satellite has 24 transponders and will be used for telecommunications and television broadcasts. Coverage will include Europe, the Mediterranean basin and central Asia.</p>
</text>
